From 110cc9cf1f007152f3bd485f6ce87248a0b7ba6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:19:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: enable the subgroup extensions instead of requiring
 them

The shader that packs the transport in one pass takes the value of the
neighbouring pixel with subgroupQuadSwapHorizontal(), and its prelude
required GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic and _quad. libplacebo writes a
custom prelude into every stage of the program, the vertex shader too,
and a driver can offer subgroups to some stages only: Mesa's zink
reports them for fragment and compute shaders (supported stages 0xe2),
and its compiler refuses the "require" in the vertex shader. The
renderer had already checked the fragment stage, so the direct way was
tried, did not compile, and was given up for the run.

With "enable" a stage that lacks the extension only gets a warning.
Where the fragment shader lacks it, the swap is not declared and the
shader does not compile, as before: nothing is drawn with a wrong
value.

Nothing changes on a driver that has the extensions in every stage,
which is every GPU the direct way has run on so far (nvidia and
radeonsi here, iris in the Intel fork).

Found when running the renderer on a software OpenGL ES, where this
change is what lets the direct way be executed and compared with the
composed one (zink on lavapipe, Mesa 26.0.8).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 06bc75b..b859e2f 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -39,9 +39,14 @@ static struct pl_hook_res pack_active_area(void *priv, const struct pl_hook_para
          .data=mask->packets, .dynamic=true},
         {.var=pl_var_uint("packet_count"), .data=&mask->count, .dynamic=true},
         {.var=pl_var_uint("flip_y"), .data=&mask->flip, .dynamic=true}};
+    /* Hades: "enable", not "require". libplacebo writes the prelude into every stage of the
+     * program, and a driver may have subgroups in fragment shaders only (Mesa's zink reports
+     * that): "require" then fails the vertex shader, and with it the whole direct way, on a GPU
+     * that could draw it. Where the fragment shader does not have them, the swap below is not
+     * declared and the shader does not compile: the frame is drawn the other way, as before. */
     struct pl_custom_shader shader = {
-        .prelude="#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : require\n"
-                 "#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_quad : require\n",
+        .prelude="#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_basic : enable\n"
+                 "#extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_quad : enable\n",
         .input=PL_SHADER_SIG_COLOR, .output=PL_SHADER_SIG_COLOR,
         .description="Exact full-raster DV transport without intermediate image",
         .variables=vars, .num_variables=4,
-- 
